<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Deva dynasty of Bengal</h1><p class="st-meta">1200 CE – 1290 CE (approx.) · capital Suvarnagrama</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Hindu dynasty of south-eastern Bengal that ruled from the Dhaka region in the 13th century, after the Sena dynasty withdrew from the west.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Deva dynasty is known almost entirely from a few <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>-plate inscriptions. It arose in the early 13th century in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikrampur">Vikrampur</a> and the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sonargaon">Suvarnagrama</a> (Sonargaon), as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sena-dynasty">Sena</a> power collapsed in western Bengal after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakhtiyar-khalji">Bakhtiyar Khalji's</a> conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nabadwip">Nadia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Dasharathadeva, the best-known king, styled himself supreme ruler and held the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhaka">Dhaka</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comilla">Comilla</a> region; his inscriptions mention the capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sonargaon">Suvarnagrama</a>. The kings were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaishnavism">Vaishnava</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindus</a> who made land grants to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmins</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a>. Little else is known of their administration or economy.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The dynasty disappears from the record in the late 13th century, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sonargaon">Sonargaon</a> came under the control of Muslim governors of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaur">Lakhnauti</a> and eventually the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>. Sonargaon later became the capital of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sonargaon-sultanate">Sonargaon Sultanate</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1200 CE – 1290 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:83.58%;width:1.79%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1200 CE – 1290 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Suvarnagrama</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Dasharathadeva</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sanskrit, Bengali</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/bangladesh">Bangladesh</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Later Deva dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1245&amp;focus=deva-dynasty-of-bengal" aria-label="Deva dynasty of Bengal on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7062 1289 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Deva dynasty of Bengal lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7358 1570h0M7018 1385h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7382 1545h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7382 1545h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Bangladesh. <a href="/atlas?year=1245&amp;focus=deva-dynasty-of-bengal">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
